{
  "_format": {
    "description": "AgentState derivation (docs/protocol.md 5.4): pure function reduce(prev, event, now). Each case starts from a fresh reducer (state idle, no pending approvals, turn_active false, last_event_at = t 0). Steps are applied in order: first all timers up to t_ms fire, then `input` (null = timers only) is applied, then the reducer output must contain every key listed in `expect`.",
    "input": {
      "kind": "AgentEvent.kind",
      "detail": "AgentEvent.detail subset",
      "actor": "AgentEvent.actor subset",
      "channel": "AgentEvent.source.channel (defaults to claude_code.hook.http)"
    },
    "expect": {
      "state": "AgentState string",
      "stale": "bool",
      "ended": "bool",
      "turn_active": "bool",
      "pending_approval_ids": "request ids in arrival order"
    },
    "conventions": [
      "Underlying (base) state follows the table; error latches (tool/command failure 5 s, test_failed 30 s, turn_failed/agent_error sticky) only overlay it, so releasing a latch reveals the base state. Pending approvals overlay everything and are the only thing that can hold awaiting_approval.",
      "Latch expiry: a 5 s / 30 s latch is active while now < start + 5000 / 30000 ms and gone at exactly start + duration.",
      "A 5 s latch is also cleared by the next *_started event (tool_started, command_started, test_run, subagent_started, review_started, turn_started) or prompt_submitted; a 30 s latch by test_passed, turn_completed, prompt_submitted; a sticky latch only by prompt_submitted.",
      "A failing test run emits command_failed and test_failed; when both latches exist the longer one wins.",
      "approval_resolved returns to the state before the first pending approval (pre_approval_state); denied_and_stopped returns idle.",
      "Codex thread/status/changed has no AgentEvent kind of its own: the normaliser emits kind 'notification' with detail {notification_type:'codex_thread_status', status, active_flags, has_recent_items?}.",
      "Codex fileChange items are tool_started with detail.item_type 'fileChange'; Codex hooks use detail.tool_name (UNVERIFIED C10).",
      "command_completed, tool_completed, subagent_*, task_*, token_usage_updated, session_meta_updated and unknown notifications do not change the state.",
      "Timers: completed -> idle after 60 s; stale = turn_active && no event for 15 min (state kept); disconnected = turn_active && 45 min, or !turn_active && 30 min without events; any event clears stale and revives a disconnected session."
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
